{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And you shall make the boards.</b> It should have said וְעָשִׂיתָ קְרָשִׁים, as is said for every single thing. What is 'the boards'? — from those that stood set aside for this. Our father Jacob planted cedars in Egypt, and when he died he commanded his sons to bring them up with them when they would leave Egypt, and he told them that the Holy One, blessed be He, was destined to command them to make a Mishkan in the wilderness of shittim wood — see that they would be ready in your hands. This is what the Babylonian established in his piyyut: 'He flew, planted, prepared — beams for our houses, cedars' — that they were prepared to be in their hands beforehand." "<b>Boards of shittim wood standing.</b> איתשט\"נביש בְּלַעַ\"ז; that the length of the boards should be upright above in the walls of the Mishkan, and you shall not make the walls with boards lying down, so that the width of the boards becomes the height of the walls, board upon board."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French estant debout / estant devis, 'standing upright'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:46.155355342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}